cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this skill or its bundled reference materials, please cite it and the relevant upstream sources below."
title: "Select LLM Agent Skill"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - name: "Ranch Forge contributors"
abstract: >-
  A reusable agent skill for selecting LLMs for tasks and agent roles by
  balancing cost, quality, and performance under budget, latency, reliability,
  provider, and deployment constraints. Supports role-aware routing for coding
  agents and multi-agent systems with structured recommendation output.
keywords:
  - llm-selection
  - model-routing
  - cost-optimization
  - agent-skills
  - prompt-engineering
  - coding-agents
references:
  - type: article
    title: "NIST AI 200-1: AI Use Taxonomy — A Human-Centered Approach"
    authors:
      - family-names: Theofanos
        given-names: Mary
      - family-names: Choong
        given-names: Yee-Yin
      - family-names: Jensen
        given-names: Theodore
    year: 2024
    doi: "10.6028/NIST.AI.200-1"
    notes: >-
      Vendored in references/NIST.AI.200-1.md and used as the activity-oriented
      taxonomy for classifying how an AI system contributes to a human task.
  - type: article
    title: "The Definitive LLM Selection & Benchmarks Guide"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://iternal.ai/llm-selection-guide"
    notes: >-
      Vendored in references/iternal-llm-selection-guide-2026.md and used as the
      capability-oriented taxonomy for determining how much model intelligence a
      task requires.
  - type: website
    title: "Artificial Analysis"
    url: "https://artificialanalysis.ai/"
    notes: >-
      The default live data source for current model pricing, availability,
      context limits, and provider compatibility. The skill includes a
      scripts/fetch-model-catalog.py helper and a snapshot fallback in
      assets/model-catalog.snapshot.json.
